  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nSOFO & IWAW\n\nSince 2020, SOFO Museum has been working with Iraqi Women Art and War (IWAW) and in 2021 received a Creative Collections Grant from South East Museum Development to further our exciting partnership.\nThe aim of the project was to welcome a new community into the museum through a series of workshops culminating in a co-curated trail of original (handmade) objects created in response to some of stories and objects held in the museums’ permeant galleries.\n\nOver the course of several months, three workshops were held at the museum and facilitated by IWAW founder and Director Rana Ibrahim and the Museum Director, Ursula Corcoran. All of the art work produced during the workshops was exhibited at the museum and reflected the impact of conflict in recent years.\n\nThe resulting art work also included a trail of clay objects created by the refugee women who took part in the project. These are currently on display in the museum with English and Arabic labels.\n\nYou can find out more about IWAW here\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
